{title: 561 - We Plow the Fields}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #561 • WIR PFLUGEN • 7.5.6.6}
{lyricist: Matthias Claudius}
{composer: Johann A. P. Schulz}
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 561}
{meta: tune WIR PFLUGEN}
{meta: meter 7.5.6.6}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]We [Ab]plow [Eb]the [Cm]fields, [Eb]and [Cm]scatter
[Ab]The [Eb/Bb]good seed [Ab]onthe [Fm]land,
[Eb/Bb]But [Fm/C]it [Bbm/F]isfed [Cm/G]and [Eb]wa tered
[Ab]By [Db/Ab]God’s [Gdim]almighty [Ab]hand.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Eb]All [Ab]good [Eb]gifts [Fm]around [Bbm]us
[Eb/Bb]Are [Ab]sent from heaven above;
[Eb]Then [Cm/Eb]thank [Eb7]the [Eb]Lord, [Ab]O [Gdim]thank [Ab]the [Cm]Lord
[Ab]For [Db/Ab]all [Fm/C]His [Eb/Bb]love.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]He [Ab]only [Eb]is the [Cm]Maker [Eb]of [Db]all [Cm]things [Bbm]near [Ab]and [Eb]far;
[Ab]He paints [Eb/Bb]the wayside [Bbm]flower, [Ab]He lights [Gdim]the evening [Eb]star.
[Eb/Bb]The winds [Fm/C]and waves [Bbm/F]obey [Cm/G]Him, by [Eb]Him the birds are [Ab]fed;
[Ab]Much more, [Db/Ab]to us [Gdim]His children, [Ab]He gives [Gdim]our [Ab]daily [Gdim]bread.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]We [Ab]thank Thee [Eb]then, O [Cm]Father, [Eb]for [Db]all [Cm]things [Bbm]bright [Ab]and [Eb]good,
[Ab]The seed-time [Eb/Bb]and [Bbm]the [Eb/Bb]harvest, [Ab]our life, [Gdim]our [Fm]health, and [Eb]food.
[Eb/Bb]Accept [Fm/C]the gifts we [Bbm/F]to [Ab]offer [Cm/G]for [Eb]all Thy love imparts,
[Ab]And, what [Db/Ab]Thou [Gdim]most desirest, [Ab]our humble, [Gdim]thankful hearts.
{end_of_verse}
